  "_doc": "The study usage ledger, <output>/.bristlenose/usage.jsonl (bristlenose/llm/usage.py, docs/design-llm-usage.md). Written by Python; read by Python and, once a surface shows it, by the Mac app. Both readers must turn `lines` into exactly `expected_rows` rows and `expected_totals`: skip blank and unreadable lines, drop a row whose row_id was already seen (a restore appends rows the Re-analyse carry already copied), and sum the rest per (provider, model) in order of first appearance, `jobs` being the distinct run ids. Tokens only: nothing here is a price.",
